// analyze-video's deliverable is a FORMULA FILE, not a render. Everything that
// separates it from the video cloner is "repeatable" against "this one, finished".
{"intent":"break down what makes this creator's videos work and write it down so we can repeat it","expected_skill":"analyze-video"}
{"intent":"I want a formula for this style, not a single prompt","expected_skill":"analyze-video"}
{"intent":"study this reference and add the style to our prompt library","expected_skill":"analyze-video"}
{"intent":"what is the structure of this ad — pacing, camera, cuts — so we can run it weekly","expected_skill":"analyze-video"}
{"intent":"save this look so we can drop any product into it later","expected_skill":"analyze-video"}
// Indirect: the ask is repeatability, phrased as a volume problem.
{"intent":"we need forty of these a month and I can't brief each one from scratch","expected_skill":"analyze-video"}
// The sibling boundary, and why it is one: same source video, two deliverables.
// "Keep making" is the template; one product, rendered, is the clone.
{"intent":"I want to keep making videos like this one","expected_skill":"analyze-video","ambiguous_with":["clone-video-ad"]}
